data: {"message": "\n\nKey risks disclosed in the 2024 Form 10-K span market exposure, supply chain and geopolitical conditions, product and intellectual property, cybersecurity, and operational strategy.\n\n- **Market and foreign exchange risk:** The company is a net receiver of currencies other than the U.S. dollar, so a strengthening dollar negatively affects net sales and gross margins. At a 95% confidence interval, the maximum one-day value-at-risk loss on foreign currency derivatives was $538 million as of September 28, 2024, versus $669 million in 2023. A hypothetical 100 basis point increase in interest rates would decrease the investment portfolio's fair value by $2,755 million and increase annual term debt interest expense by $139 million in 2024.\n- **Supply chain concentration and geopolitical exposure:** Substantially all manufacturing is outsourced to partners primarily in China mainland, India, Japan, South Korea, Taiwan and Vietnam. Trade restrictions, tariffs or disputes\u2014particularly between the U.S. and China\u2014could increase costs and force expensive, disruptive supply chain changes. The company relies on single or limited sources for many critical components, and operations are exposed to earthquakes, natural disasters, public health issues and climate change.\n- **Product quality, liability and inventory:** Design and manufacturing defects, including in third-party components and new technologies like artificial intelligence, can lead to recalls, product liability claims, asset write-offs and warranty expenses. Inventory obsolescence and purchase commitment cancellation risks persist given rapid technology changes; manufacturing purchase obligations typically cover periods up to 150 days.\n- **Intellectual property:** Products rely on third-party intellectual property that may not be available on commercially reasonable terms or at all, and the company risks unknowingly infringing existing patents, which could require product modifications or preclude sales.\n- **Cybersecurity and IT:** Malicious attacks occur regularly and are expected to accelerate in frequency and sophistication; security measures remain vulnerable to ransomware, employee error and supplier breaches, and insurance may not cover all losses. IT system failures or network disruptions could impede manufacturing, shipping and access to online services.\n- **Talent, channels and strategy:** Success depends on retaining key personnel amid intense competition, particularly in Silicon Valley. Distribution depends on carriers, wholesalers and resellers, many of which sell competitor products, and reseller financing or support could weaken. Acquisitions or new business strategies carry risks of impairment, write-offs and management distraction, while retail stores face lease, construction and inventory value risks.\n\nSource: apple 10k.pdf, p. 9, 12, 14, 15, 30.", "model": "openai", "success": true, "tickers": [], "intents": ["RISK_ANALYSIS"], "sources": [{"document_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9", "filename": "apple 10k.pdf", "page": 30, "chunk_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9:000029", "score": -4.899998188018799}, {"document_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9", "filename": "apple 10k.pdf", "page": 12, "chunk_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9:000011", "score": -5.784700870513916}, {"document_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9", "filename": "apple 10k.pdf", "page": 15, "chunk_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9:000014", "score": -6.420445919036865}, {"document_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9", "filename": "apple 10k.pdf", "page": 9, "chunk_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9:000008", "score": -6.891432285308838}, {"document_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9", "filename": "apple 10k.pdf", "page": 14, "chunk_id": "dc62d42da64f47379dca22417c445dd9:000013", "score": -6.98444128036499}]}

